         <div type="bio">
            <p>Swiss painter, illustrator and satirical cartoonist. Born Georges-Charles Augsburger in Yverdon-les-Bains in French Switzerland, Augsbourg visited JJ in Saint-Gérard-le-Puy in November 1940 and offered to help getting <name type="person" key="joyc07">Lucia</name> into Switzerland. Augsbourg exhibited at the progressive Salon des Surindépendants in 1929 but is best known today for his collaboration with <name type="person" key="ID_MISSING">Jean Cocteau</name> on <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">La vie de Darius Milhaud en images</name> (1935). For many years he edited and contributed to the <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Journal de la Maison Charles Veillon</name>. <hi rend="bold">Ronan Crowley</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
